    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1149-a1">

                <pb facs="1038" n="724" xml:id="pg724"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. Your 310, 25th. You should not issue passports to declarants of German
                    birth. Law does not authorize issuance of passports to wives of declarants.
                    Consuls may register and furnish them certificates specifying their status. Ask
                    permission of German Government for their, departure with such certificates in
                    lieu of passports.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
